}You are stridently aligned.		<-- Q: What does this mean?

It means you have not violated your alignment.  The other
possibilities are "You are nominally aligned" (bad) or "You have
strayed" (very bad--on your God's shitlist).

}You are poison resistant.		<-- Intrinsic

Just a nit pick about terminology--these are all intrinsics, not just
the ones you get from eating corpses.  Attributes you get from rings,
alignment, etc. are also intrinsics.

}Bad luck does not time out for you.	<-- Q: What do these mean?
}Good luck does not time out for you.	<-- 

These are the effects of an uncursed luckstone.  If you have a blessed
luckstone, only good luck does not time out.  If you have a cursed
luckstone, only bad luck does not time out (and you can't drop it).

}Two more questions: 
}Seems shops never appear at deep levels, is it supposed so?

Yes.  You don't run into shops when you're (presumedly) powerful
enough to kill shopkeeper as easily as you squash a bug.  The odds of
running into a shop are inversely proportional to the dungeon level.

}What's the use of gems besides selling them for money?

Two things that I know of:

If you finish the game with gems, you get their value in points, and
real gems (not worthless pieces of <color> glass) have better
value/weight ratios than gold.

If you throw gems at coaligned unicorns, you gain luck.  1 point for
an unidentified gem, 5 points for an identified real gem, and a the
unicorn's scorn for an identified worthless piece of glass.

